CORE broken-z3-smt-backend broken-cprover-smt-backend no-new-smt
conversions.c
--cvc5
^\[main\.assertion\.[0-9]+\] line \d+ fails: FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Conversions between mathematical integers and bit-vectors or floats with the
SMT2 back-end. All assertions but the one labelled "fails" hold. Z3 4.8 cannot
decide int2bv and to_fp of a non-constant real in reasonable time (or answers
unknown), hence this uses CVC5.
